From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000002 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Wig Cheng <wigcheng@ieiworld.com>
Date: Wed, 20 May 2026 14:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] tsntool: fix conflicting declaration of wait_tsn_multicast

The header declares wait_tsn_multicast() with an empty parameter list,
while its definition in multicast.c takes a struct alarm_info * argument.

GCC 15 in Ubuntu 26.04 defaults to -std=gnu23, under which the empty
() in a function declaration is interpreted as (void) rather than the
pre-C23 "unspecified parameters" meaning. The build then fails with a
conflicting-types error between the declaration and the definition.

Forward-declare struct alarm_info and update the prototype to match
the actual signature used in the implementation.

Upstream-Status: Pending
Signed-off-by: Wig Cheng <wigcheng@ieiworld.com>
---
 include/tsn/genl_tsn.h | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/include/tsn/genl_tsn.h b/include/tsn/genl_tsn.h
--- a/include/tsn/genl_tsn.h
+++ b/include/tsn/genl_tsn.h
@@ -457,6 +457,7 @@ pthread_t *create_alarm_common(uint64_t ts, uint32_t offset, uint32_t cycle,
 			      void (*callback_func)(void *data), void *data);
 int delete_alarm_common(pthread_t *thread);
-int wait_tsn_multicast();
+struct alarm_info;
+int wait_tsn_multicast(struct alarm_info *ainfo);
 void get_para_from_json(int type, cJSON *json, void *para);

 bool get_conf_monitor_status(void);
-- 
